#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see four clear peaks at `00000000`, `01000000`, `10000000`, and "
"`11000000`, with some counts in other bitstrings due to noise in the quantum"
" computer. We'll ignore these and keep only the dominant four by imposing a "
"threshold: only counts above this threshold are considered a true signal "
"above the noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakikita natin ang apat na malinaw na tuktok sa `00000000`, `01000000`, "
"`10000000`, at `11000000`, na may ilang bilang sa iba pang mga bitstring "
"dahil sa ingay sa quantum computer. Ibibukod natin ang mga ito at iingatan "
"lang ang nangingibabaw na apat sa pamamagitan ng pagtatakda ng threshold: "
"ang mga bilang na nasa itaas ng threshold na ito lamang ang itinuturing na "
"tunay na signal na higit sa ingay.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Post-process {#4-post-process}"
msgstr "4. Post-process {#4-post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For Shor's algorithm, quite a lot of the algorithm is performed classically."
" So, we'll put the rest of it in the \"post-processing\" step, after we've "
"gotten our measurements from the quantum computer. Each of the measurements "
"above can be converted into integers, which, after we divide by $2^m$, are "
"our approximations for $\\frac{k}{r}$, where $k$ is random each time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa Shor's algorithm, malaking bahagi ng algorithm ay isinasagawa nang "
"klasikal. Kaya, ilalagay natin ang natitirang bahagi sa hakbang na \"post-"
"processing,\" pagkatapos makuha ang ating mga sukat mula sa quantum "
"computer. Ang bawat isa sa mga sukat sa itaas ay maaaring i-convert sa mga "
"integer, na, pagkatapos nating hatiin sa $2^m$, ay ating mga pagtatantya "
"para sa $\\frac{k}{r}$, kung saan ang $k$ ay random sa bawat pagkakataon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Konklusyon {#conclusion}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After going through the module, you may be struck with a new appreciation of"
" the brilliance of Peter Shor to have come up with such a clever algorithm. "
"But hopefully you've also reached a new level of understanding of its "
"deceptive simplicity. Although the algorithm may seem impressively (or "
"intimidatingly) complex, if you break it down into each step of logic and go"
" through it slowly, you, too, will be able to run Shor's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos dumaan sa module na ito, maaaring magkaroon ka ng bagong "
"pagpapahalaga sa katalinuhan ni Peter Shor na makagawa ng ganoong matalinong"
" algorithm. Ngunit sana ay nakarating ka na rin sa isang bagong antas ng "
"pag-unawa sa kanyang mapanlinlang na kasimplihan. Kahit na mukhang kahanga-"
"hanga (o nakakatakot) ang algorithm, kung hahati-hatiin mo ito sa bawat "
"hakbang ng lohika at dahan-dahang dadaanan, ikaw din ay makakapagtakbo ng "
"Shor's algorithm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While we're far from using this algorithm to factor numbers like RSA1024, "
"our quantum computers are getting better every day, and once a threshold "
"called *fault tolerance* is reached, then algorithms such as these will be "
"soon to follow. It's an exciting time to be learning about quantum "
"computing!\n"
msgstr ""
"Malayo pa tayo sa paggamit ng algorithm na ito para i-factor ang mga bilang "
"tulad ng RSA1024, ngunit ang aming mga quantum computer ay nagiging mas "
"mahusay araw-araw, at kapag naabot na ang isang threshold na tinatawag na "
"*fault tolerance*, ang mga algorithm na tulad nito ay malapit nang sumunod. "
"Kapana-panabik na panahon ito para matuto tungkol sa quantum computing!\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Problems {#problems}"
msgstr "Mga Problema {#problems}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Mga kritikal na konsepto: {#critical-concepts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern cryptographic systems rely on the classical difficulty of factoring "
"large integers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga modernong cryptographic system ay umaasa sa klasikal na kahirapan ng"
" pag-factor ng malalaking integer.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modular arithmetic — including the structures $\\mathbb{Z}_N$ and "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_N^*$ — provides the mathematical foundation for Shor’s "
"algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang modular arithmetic — kabilang ang mga istruktura ng $\\mathbb{Z}_N$ at "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_N^*$ — ay nagbibigay ng mathematical na pundasyon para sa "
"Shor's algorithm.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The problem of factoring an integer $N$ can be reduced to the problem of "
"finding the order of a number modulo $N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang problema ng pag-factor ng integer na $N$ ay maaaring bawasan sa problema"
" ng paghanap ng order ng isang numero modulo $N$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum order finding uses quantum phase estimation techniques to determine "
"the period of the function $a^x \\mod N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang quantum order finding ay gumagamit ng mga quantum phase estimation "
"technique para matukoy ang period ng function na $a^x \\mod N$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor’s algorithm consists of a classical–quantum hybrid workflow that "
"selects a base, performs quantum order finding, and then classically "
"computes the factors from the result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Shor's algorithm ay binubuo ng isang klasikal–quantum hybrid workflow na"
" pumipili ng base, nagsasagawa ng quantum order finding, at pagkatapos ay "
"klasikal na kinakalkula ang mga factor mula sa resulta.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "True/False: {#truefalse}"
msgstr "Tama/Mali: {#truefalse}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The efficiency of Shor's algorithm threatens the security of RSA "
"encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/M Ang kahusayan ng Shor's algorithm ay nagbabanta sa seguridad ng RSA "
"encryption.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F Shor's algorithm can be executed efficiently on any modern-day quantum "
"computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/M Ang Shor's algorithm ay maaaring maisakatuparan nang mahusay sa anumang "
"makabagong quantum computer ngayon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F Shor’s algorithm uses quantum phase estimation (QPE) as a key "
"subroutine.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/M Ang Shor's algorithm ay gumagamit ng quantum phase estimation (QPE) "
"bilang isang pangunahing subroutine.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The classical part of Shor’s algorithm involves calculating the greatest"
" common divisor (GCD).\n"
msgstr ""
"T/M Ang klasikal na bahagi ng Shor's algorithm ay kinabibilangan ng "
"pagkalkula ng greatest common divisor (GCD).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Shor’s algorithm only works for factoring even numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/M Ang Shor's algorithm ay gumagana lamang para sa pag-factor ng mga pantay"
" na bilang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F A successful run of Shor’s algorithm always guarantees the correct "
"factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/M Ang isang matagumpay na pagtakbo ng Shor's algorithm ay palaging "
"ginagarantiyahang tama ang mga factor.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Short answer: {#short-answer}"
msgstr "Maikling sagot: {#short-answer}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why is Shor’s algorithm considered a potential future threat to RSA "
"encryption?\n"
msgstr ""
"Bakit itinuturing na isang potensyal na banta sa hinaharap ang Shor's "
"algorithm sa RSA encryption?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why is finding the period, or order, of a modular exponential function "
"helpful for factoring a number in Shor’s algorithm?\n"
msgstr ""
"Bakit nakakatulong ang paghanap ng period, o order, ng isang modular "
"exponential function para sa pag-factor ng isang numero sa Shor's "
"algorithm?\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Challenge problems: {#challenge-problems}"
msgstr "Mga hamon na problema: {#challenge-problems}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How many control qubits $m$ do we need for a given number $N$ that we're "
"trying to factor to obtain the precision in the QPE needed to find the "
"correct value of the order $r$?\n"
msgstr ""
"Ilang control qubit na $m$ ang kailangan natin para sa isang ibinigay na "
"bilang na $N$ na sinusubukan nating i-factor para makuha ang precision sa "
"QPE na kinakailangan para mahanap ang tamang value ng order na $r$?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following the procedure we outlined here to factor 15, now try to factor "
"21.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinusunod ang pamamaraan na aming binalangkas dito para i-factor ang 15, "
"subukan mo ngayong i-factor ang 21.\n"
